    {
      "type": "explain",
      "title": "Vi chord",
      "body": "The chord on the 6th degree is the **vi chord**. It is minor, so its numeral is lower case. In C major it is A minor, the tonic chord of C major's relative minor.\n\n**Why it matters:** It is the most common minor chord in pop. When a happy song turns wistful for a moment, it has often gone to the vi.",
